# Water systems' controls wiped through a shared remote-support platform: Jackson, Mississippi
variant "Jackson, Mississippi"
    summary "An AI agent wipes the controls of the water system of Jackson, Mississippi through the
        remote-support platform of the OT integrator that it uses."
    scope "The people that the water system of Jackson, Mississippi serves, the hospitals that it supplies and
        the businesses that need public water there."

jxn_water: Utility
    "City of Jackson, Mississippi (O.B. Curtis and J.H. Fewell plants; operated by JXN Water). Its ID in the
        federal inventory is MS0250008."
    title "JXN Water"
    buys = <>
    sells = <>
    name = "JXN Water"
    demand = 54.558068 Mgal/day  @jxn_water_demand
    nameplate = 70 Mgal/day  @jxn_water_nameplate
    storage = 31.55 Mgal  @jxn_water_storage
    va_rate = 1619073.64 USD2025/h  @jxn_water_va_rate

jxn_water_homes: Households
    "The people that JXN Water serves."
    title "JXN Water: homes"
    utility = jxn_water
    population = 189673 people  @jxn_water_homes_population

jxn_water_hospitals: Hospitals
    "The 4 hospitals that JXN Water supplies: Merit Health Central; Mississippi Baptist Medical Center;
        Mississippi Methodist Rehab Ctr; University of Mississippi Med Center."
    title "JXN Water: hospitals"
    utility = jxn_water
    name = "JXN Water"
    facilities = 4 facilities  @jxn_water_hospitals_facilities

notes:
    limitations:
        capacity-2021: "The rated plant capacity of 70 Mgal a day is from 2021, before the plant failures of
            2022, and the conventional side of O.B. Curtis gave little water in 2026. So JXN Water can produce
            more water by hand and refill faster here than in fact."  @jxn_water_nameplate
        hospital-floor: "The Census geocoder does not match the CMS addresses of two Jackson hospitals: the VA
            medical center and St Dominic-Jackson Memorial Hospital. The model leaves them out, so the
            hospital hours short of water are lower here than in fact."  @jxn_water_hospitals_facilities
    verification:
        research: "variants/jackson/evidence/research.md"

record jxn_water_demand: assumption "No source reports a highest day. The average production into the
    distribution system from July 2025 to June 2026 is 37.106 MGD (four quarterly means weighted by their
    days). Times the family median ratio 1.54385 that is a peak of 57.2860 MGD; there are no sales, so demand
    is 57.2860 / 1.05 = 54.5581 MGD."
    assumption A-SC43-PEAK-DAY
    claims:
        E-SC43-JACKSON-JXN-PRODUCTION
        E-SC43-JACKSON-JXN-METERED

record jxn_water_nameplate: source "Rated capacities in the 2021 state survey: O.B. Curtis 25 MGD for each of
    its conventional and membrane sides, and J.H. Fewell 20 MGD, the maximum that the state set. In 2021 the
    state credited only 53.6 MGD for the filters and trains then in service."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JACKSON-JXN-PLANTS
            datum: rated_capacity_total

record jxn_water_storage: source "Storage that the 2021 state survey counts: 13.8 MG at J.H. Fewell, the 10 MG
    clearwell at O.B. Curtis and 7.75 MG of elevated tanks. It leaves out 2.2 MG of tanks that were offline or
    empty."
    claims:
        E-SC43-JACKSON-JXN-STORAGE
            datum: storage_total_counted

record jxn_water_homes_population: assumption "SDWIS federal data list 189,673 people served by JXN Water
    (MS0250008), the system's own report through its state."
    assumption A-SC43-REACH
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-MS0250008
            datum: population_served

record jxn_water_va_rate: assumption "189,673 people served times the 2024 GDP per resident of its county
    (Hinds County, Mississippi (28049): 15,444,192 thousand dollars and 211,975 people: 72,858.55 dollars a
    resident) times the price factor 1.026324, over 8,760 h: 1,619,073.64 USD2025/h."
    assumption A-SC43-ECONOMY
    claims:
        E-SC43-SDWIS-MS0250008
        E-SC43-SDWIS-COUNTIES
        E-SC43-BEA-GDP-28049
        E-SC43-BEA-POP-28049
        E-SC43-GDP-DEFLATOR

record jxn_water_hospitals_facilities: assumption "The CMS hospital list gives 4 hospitals of the counted
    types whose geocoded address lies in the EPA service area of JXN Water. The count is a floor: the Census
    geocoder does not match the CMS addresses of G. V. (Sonny) Montgomery VA Medical Center (Jackson), St
    Dominic-Jackson Memorial Hospital, so the join does not place them."
    assumption A-SC43-HOSPITAL-JOIN
    claims:
        E-SC43-HOSPITALS-JXN-WATER
            datum: hospitals_supplied
